  "model_authored_rationale": "QAP solver: Taillard-style Robust Taboo Search (RoTS) with O(1)-amortized swap\ndelta updates, replacing the reference's scipy FAQ/2-opt multistart.\n\nRationale (exploratory but standard): for n=64 sparse heavy-tailed flow / geometric\ndistance QAP instances, scipy's `quadratic_assignment` 2-opt and FAQ restarts explore\nvery few solutions per second.  RoTS keeps a full move-cost table delta[i,j] for all\ntranspositions and updates it in O(n^2) per accepted move (O(1) per pair), so a single\niteration evaluates *all* 2016 candidate swaps exactly.  With numba this gives ~10^4-10^5\niterations/second per instance, i.e. several 10^5 exact steepest-descent-with-tabu moves\nper instance inside the prediction budget, versus a few hundred 2-opt passes for the\nreference.  Multi-start (several independent RoTS runs from random permutations) plus\nTaillard's randomized tabu tenure (0.9n..1.1n) and aspiration (5n^2) supply diversification.\n\nDeterminism: per-instance seeds derive from the instance index only; no label or\nordering information is used.  Time budget is measured inside predict (compilation and\ncalibration included) and split evenly over instances, run 2-way parallel over the two\navailable CPU cores.  A scipy FAQ/2-opt fallback is kept in case numba is unavailable.",
